WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:02.350
Last question today, David.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:05.740
Why are older voters abandoning Trump?

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:12.610
Last week, you talked about why rural white,
older voters like Trump, but now they're abandoning

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:13.610
him.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:18.820
Why is it basically three reasons appear to
be what's going what's really hurting Donald

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.140
Trump in the last week?

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.260
This is new.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.860
Before this week, we knew Trump's handling
of Corona virus was hurting him in general

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.990
and hurting him with older voters.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.640
Trump's handling of the economy as a result
of coronavirus meaning the economic destruction

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.690
was worse than it had to be because of Trump's
mishandling of corona virus that is hurting

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.199
Trump with older voters.

00:00:40.199 --> 00:00:44.249
But we now, in addition, have the issue of
debate performance.

00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:50.019
The post debate polls by Donald Trump, the
post debate polls that account for Donald

00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:51.019
Trump.

00:00:51.019 --> 00:00:56.979
Trump's performance in the debate are a disaster
for Trump, specifically among older voters.

00:00:56.979 --> 00:01:05.019
Older voters in some polls are no longer even
the demographic group age wise that most supports

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:06.019
Trump.

00:01:06.019 --> 00:01:11.689
There is a new poll, I think it was the CNN
poll from this week where the under 35 crowd

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:15.280
is actually Trump's strongest group.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.960
From the standpoint of age and what's going
on is that for a lot of older folks, corona

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.880
virus is not abstract.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.900
Certainly, if you're in a nursing home and
you see people dying and you see the chaos,

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.560
it is not numbers you check once a day.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.539
It is very real.

00:01:33.539 --> 00:01:40.210
If you simply know people not nursing home
related who aren't doing well and of course,

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:43.729
because it disproportionately affects older
folks, those are the folks most likely to

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:47.740
have friends and people in their circle that
are suffering directly.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:52.140
And then you see Trump go on television and
say it's like a flu.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.439
It's no big deal.

00:01:53.439 --> 00:01:54.439
We've turned the corner.

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:57.149
Our mark, we're getting great marks.

00:01:57.149 --> 00:02:03.280
You see the obvious lies and you know, well,
you know, Blanch died and Joe died.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.840
How is Trump saying this?

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:08.170
Your friends are in ICU use.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.980
That is going to create a problem for you.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.300
And then went on top of it.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:16.310
You start looking at your retirement account
or you're on a fixed income or Trump's talking

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:20.590
about cutting funding to Social Security by
a payroll tax deferral.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.000
It's not good.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.670
And pretending that this was a hoax was a
very bad idea.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.300
The statistics don't lie.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:33.410
We said in May when Trump started transitioning
into we beat it, that that might work in June

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:37.180
and July, but it's not going to work forever
and it's not been working.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:38.180
And then you.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:43.880
Add to the fact that Hillary Clinton was less
liked than Joe Biden.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:52.780
Joe Biden, by and large, particularly for
older white folks, is much more likable than

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:53.820
Hillary Clinton.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.040
He's the type of guy most people would like
to sit down and just talk to.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.130
Many older voters would identify with Joe
Biden.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:07.730
Guy who grew up working class, likes trains,
has suffered significant personal loss and

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:08.960
so on and so forth.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:14.930
Then you look at Trump and he's just a rude,
disgusting guy who yelled the entire debate.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:21.400
So all of that together tells us seniors are
paying attention.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.450
They're not willing to die for the economy.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:27.850
Like the what was his name, Dan Roberts or
Dan Patrick.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:33.720
The lieutenant governor of Texas said early
on in this thing and they're paying attention.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.720
They're paying attention to what's going on.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:41.220
Trump, already going into all of this, was
doing less well with seniors than many previous

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.250
Republicans had done.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.550
Now it's gotten even worse.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:45.700
He's got the latest.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.820
Polls in the last 96 hours are very, very
bad.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:54.540
And hopefully every single one of these groups
will completely repudiate Donald Trump in

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.650
a brutal, brutal defeat.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.270
But it's up to us to make it happen.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.160
And we're going to try to do that.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:01.160
Exactly.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:05.710
And we will continue pushing next week and
the week after and the week after that.

